{"id":57536998288677,"type":"artist","name":"Bobby Vinton","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":20,"info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Bobby_Vinton_1964.JPG?width=500","bio":"Conocido principalmente por la interpretación del gran clásico “Blue Velvet”, Bobby Vinton fue uno de los cantantes más populares en los Estados Unidos de comienzos de los años 60 gracias a su aseada imagen de teen idol, su candorosa voz, y sus baladas, cálidas, refinadas y sentimentales interpretaciones de pop vocal con dulces arreglos orquestales.\n\nBobby Vinton (de nombre real Stanley Robert Vintula) nació el 16 de abril de 1935 en la localidad de Canonsburg, en Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.","tags":["oldies","60s","pop","easy listening","male vocalists"]},"works":[{"id":183412089740878,"type":"song","name":"Roses Are Red","artist":"Bobby Vinton","year":1962,"weight":2,"yt":null,"src":"charts","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":132335824845498,"name":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","rank":4,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":65873579436799,"type":"song","name":"Roses Are Red (My Love)","artist":"Bobby Vinton","year":1962,"weight":7,"yt":"8rjPC7-JMUM","src":"ensayos,singles","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[{"name":"Hit Parade Music History and Music Trivia","n":1}],"lists":[{"id":175487015765550,"name":"Billboard Year-End 1962","rank":4,"scaruffi":null},{"id":157497903047680,"name":"Billboard Hot 100 nº1 · 1960s","rank":74,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":2}},{"id":143863784501704,"type":"album","name":"Blue Velvet","artist":"Bobby Vinton","year":1963,"weight":9,"yt":"b5IT4KiaYvc","src":"books,musthear","from":{"books":[{"name":"1966","title":"1966: The Year the Decade Exploded (Jon Savage)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":137828800833770,"name":"RYM Top — Pop — Teen Pop","rank":135,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":1}},{"id":198332555253290,"type":"song","name":"Blue Velvet","artist":"Bobby Vinton","year":1963,"weight":5,"yt":"icfq_foa5Mo","src":"charts,singles","fr